[METHOD JUSTIFICATION & LOGICAL HANDLING]
1. Cancelled/Diverted Flights:
   In accordance with FAA and Bureau of Transportation Statistics (BTS) standards,
   cancelled and diverted flights never reached their scheduled destination gate.
   Imputing an arbitrary arrival delay (e.g., 0 or mean) would severely distort delay
   metrics. They are preserved with NaN/explicit indicator for cancellation analysis.
2. Operational Flights (Sensor/Logging Dropouts):
   For active, non-cancelled flights missing arrival delay, we estimate arrival delay
   using the strong physical correlation between Departure Delay and Arrival Delay:
   Estimated Arrival Delay = Departure Delay + Median Enroute Adjustment (-3 mins).
   This domain-informed logical imputation preserves flight mechanics without adding noise.

