 TASK 11: CORRELATION ANALYSIS (DEPARTURE DELAY VS ARRIVAL DELAY)
Pearson Correlation Coefficient (Series.corr()): 0.9877

[EXPLANATION OF CORRELATION COEFFICIENT]
A correlation coefficient of r = 0.9877 indicates a VERY STRONG POSITIVE LINEAR RELATIONSHIP.
In aviation operations, this demonstrates that departure delays propagate directly into arrival
delays. While pilots can adjust cruise airspeed to recover a marginal buffer (3-7 minutes),
flights that depart significantly late almost invariably arrive late, confirming departure punctuality
as the single most critical predictor of overall flight reliability.
