2. Standard Deviation (42.2 mins):
   A high standard deviation reflects substantial schedule variance and operational volatility,
   indicating that delays fluctuate widely across different airport hubs and times.
3. 90th Percentile (65.0 mins):
   90% of all flights depart with less than 65.0 minutes of delay. In aviation planning,
   airlines use the 90th percentile as the benchmark for establishing aircraft turnaround buffers
   and passenger connection protection windows.
